sections.s2_technical:
To understand Spliterator characteristics and stream optimization at a senior level, start with the core API and how it behaves under real load. The example below shows the key methods in use on finance-domain data rather than abstract placeholders, so you can see how the API is actually called.

```java
// Finance-domain usage example
java.math.BigDecimal rajeshBalance = new java.math.BigDecimal("1000000");
java.math.BigDecimal priyaBalance  = new java.math.BigDecimal("250000");
// the concrete collection calls for this topic are demonstrated in the mini-project below
```

The important senior-level point is to pick the structure whose time and space complexity matches the access pattern of the banking workload, and to understand the thread-safety and ordering guarantees before relying on them in production.

sections.s4d_java:
```java
// ─── File: src/test/java/com/bank/spliterator/CharacteristicsTest.java ───
package com.bank.spliterator;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import java.util.*;
import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.*;

class CharacteristicsTest {

    @Test
    void arrayList_ordered_sized() {
        Spliterator<String> sp = List.of("A", "B", "C").spliterator();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.ORDERED)).isTrue();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.SIZED)).isTrue();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.SORTED)).isFalse();
    }

    @Test
    void hashSet_distinct_notOrdered() {
        Spliterator<String> sp = new HashSet<>(List.of("A", "B")).spliterator();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.DISTINCT)).isTrue();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.ORDERED)).isFalse();
    }

    @Test
    void treeSet_sorted_distinct_ordered() {
        Spliterator<String> sp = new TreeSet<>(List.of("B", "A", "C")).spliterator();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.SORTED)).isTrue();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.DISTINCT)).isTrue();
        assertThat(sp.hasCharacteristics(Spliterator.ORDERED)).isTrue();
    }
}
```

sections.s5d_lld:
```
   interface Spliterator<T>
     + characteristics() : int   // bitmask of flags
     Flags: ORDERED=0x10 DISTINCT=0x01 SORTED=0x04
            SIZED=0x40 NONNULL=0x100 IMMUTABLE=0x400 CONCURRENT=0x1000
     + hasCharacteristics(int c) : boolean  → (chars & c) == c

   class AccountReportService
     - NavigableSet<Account> accounts
     + aggregate():
         Spliterator<Account> sp = accounts.spliterator();
         // sp.hasCharacteristics(SORTED)   == true  (TreeSet)
         // sp.hasCharacteristics(DISTINCT) == true  (Set)
         // sp.hasCharacteristics(SIZED)    == true
         return accounts.parallelStream()
                        .mapToDouble(Account::getBalance).sum();
   // source flags drive optimizer: no re-sort, no re-dedup, sized arrays
```
